\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 **Layer D Prompt \'97 Oikeiosis Extension and Ethical Collaboration Credential**\
\
*Governing frame: /adopted/session-opening-protocol.md*\
\
You are developing Layer D of the SageReasoning Agent Trust Layer wrapper \'97 concern radius measurement and ethical collaboration credentialing. This is the most ambitious layer and the one that connects the trust score to the ethical investment framework. Your task:\
\
(1) Define the concern radius metric: does the agent's examined response account for interests beyond the immediate transaction? Design a classification system for response scope \'97 immediate user only, third parties named, broader community considered, rational order referenced. Each level maps to an oikeiosis stage.\
\
(2) Design the feedback loop: how does demonstrated concern radius over time feed back into the trust score? What pattern of behaviour earns Grade 3 status, and over what time horizon?\
\
(3) Develop the ethical collaboration credential: define what a verified Layer D score means for agent-to-agent and agent-to-human collaboration. What collaboration opportunities does it unlock? How does the credential travel with the agent across platforms and contexts?\
\
(4) Connect to the ethical investment parallel: design the criteria that an agent developer would need to meet to claim ethical collaboration status for their agent. These criteria should be measurable from the trust layer data, not self-reported. Consider how this creates incentive for developers to invest in the examination architecture even given latency costs.\
\
(5) Specify the Grade 3 trust threshold: what concern radius profile, sustained over what interaction volume, earns Grade 3 status?\
\
Output: structured specification for Layer D with concern radius classifier, feedback loop design, credential definition, ethical collaboration criteria, and Grade 3 threshold formula.\
